<main><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/blogs/">Travel Guides</a> / Udaipur Solo Trip</div><span class="eyebrow">Real Swiggy Wala traveller story</span><h1>3-Day Solo Udaipur Trip with Camel Safari & Local Experiences</h1><p>A real Udaipur journey combining a special camel activity with old-city exploration, lakefront heritage, local transport, cafes and a relaxed solo-travel pace.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><article class="blog-story-article"><div class="blog-story-meta"><span>Published: 14 September 2026</span><span>Destination: Udaipur, Rajasthan</span><span>Trip type: Solo</span></div><p class="article-lead">This 3-day solo Udaipur trip organised with Swiggy Wala was designed around one simple idea: experience the city instead of only ticking off attractions. A camel safari was included as a special activity, while the main journey covered Udaipur’s heritage streets, Gangaur Ghat, the Bagore Ki Haveli area, local auto rides, cafe experiences and time at Jagat Niwas Palace.</p><h2>Trip overview: what was included?</h2><p>The itinerary mixed structured experiences with flexible time. That meant the traveller could explore the old city, stop at places that felt interesting and still have clear anchors for each day. The result was a trip that felt personal rather than rushed.</p><ul><li>Special camel safari / camel experience in Udaipur</li><li>Local auto-rickshaw exploration through the city</li><li>Gangaur Ghat sunset and lakefront atmosphere</li><li>Bagore Ki Haveli and surrounding old-city heritage</li><li>Quala Cafe for food, interiors and a relaxed break</li><li>Jagat Niwas Palace heritage and breakfast experience</li><li>Evening and late-night walks through Udaipur</li></ul><h2>Camel Safari: a special activity inside the main trip</h2><p>The camel safari was not the whole itinerary; it was one highlighted activity within the broader 3-day Udaipur journey. For travellers looking for a Rajasthani touch beyond palaces and lakes, a camel experience can add variety to a customised itinerary. Availability, operating area, animal-welfare practices and current local conditions should always be confirmed before booking.</p><h2>Exploring Udaipur by local auto</h2><p>Short local auto rides made it easier to move through Udaipur’s busy streets and heritage areas without turning every transfer into a formal car movement. For solo travel, this can be a practical way to explore compact old-city zones, provided the route, fare and pickup point are agreed clearly.</p><h2>Gangaur Ghat and Bagore Ki Haveli</h2><p>Gangaur Ghat became one of the strongest atmosphere-led parts of the trip: open lake views, heritage facades, people gathering near the water and the gradual change from afternoon light to evening. The nearby Bagore Ki Haveli area added another layer of old-Udaipur character after sunset.</p><h2>Udaipur cafes and Quala Cafe</h2><p>Travel does not need to be nonstop sightseeing. A cafe break can be part of the itinerary itself, especially in Udaipur where design, heritage-inspired interiors and rooftop or courtyard settings often shape the experience. Quala Cafe was one such stop during this journey, combining food with a visually distinctive setting.</p><h2>Jagat Niwas Palace experience</h2><p>The white heritage architecture and quiet courtyards at Jagat Niwas Palace added a softer, slower mood to the itinerary. A morning or breakfast in a heritage setting can work well after a busy sightseeing day, especially for travellers who value architecture, photography and calm lake-city mornings.</p><h2>What makes a good 3-day solo Udaipur itinerary?</h2><p>A useful three-day plan should group nearby places, protect the late-afternoon sunset window and avoid spending the entire trip in transfers. Solo travellers often benefit from a mix of planned transport and flexible local movement, with clear check-in details, emergency contacts and realistic travel buffers.</p><div class="inline-cta"><h3>Plan a personalised Udaipur trip with Swiggy Wala</h3><p>Share your travel dates, pickup city, hotel preference and the experiences you want — camel activity, heritage, cafes, lakefront time or a slower solo itinerary.</p><a class="btn" href="<?=e(wa_link('Hello Swiggy Wala, I read your 3-day solo Udaipur trip story and want a personalised itinerary.'))?>" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><?=wa_icon()?>Ask for a Udaipur Plan</a></div><h2>See the real traveller story and photos</h2><p>View the visual trip story in our <a href="/stories/udaipur-solo-trip/">Udaipur solo traveller story</a> and the <a href="/gallery/">Swiggy Wala travel gallery</a>.</p><p>Traveller Instagram: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.instagram.com/debchandrima_official/">@debchandrima_official</a><br>Original Udaipur post: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.instagram.com/p/DW8I6pJDI1o/">instagram.com/p/DW8I6pJDI1o/</a></p></article></div></section></main>
